Port Guard stops devices inside the network by their MAC address: a
listed device - or every device of one maker, by the first bytes of the
address - can send nothing through the firewall and receive nothing
through it. The page lists the devices the firewall sees, each a click
from being blocked. The addresses are resolved by OPNsense's own MAC
alias and kept current; the block rules are registered by the plugin
and never added to the owner's own rules.

Two devices behind the same switch still reach each other; blocking
those needs the switch.

